{"answerArea":{"calculator":true,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"The formula for the derivative of $\\arctan(x)$ is:\n\n$\\dfrac{d}{dx}[\\arctan(x)]=\\dfrac{1}{1+x^2}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"Let's start by finding $\\dfrac{dy}{dx}$:\n\n$\\begin{align}\n\\dfrac{dy}{dx}\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[\\arctan\\left(-4x\\right)\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{1}{1+\\left(-4x\\right)^2}\\cdot\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[-4x\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{-4}{1+16x^2}\n\\end{align}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"Now we evaluate $\\dfrac{dy}{dx}$ at $\\blueD{x=3}$:\n\n$\\begin{align}\n\u0026\\phantom{=}\\dfrac{-4}{1+16\\left(\\blueD{3}\\right)^2}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{-4}{145}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-\\dfrac{4}{145}\n\\end{align}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"In conclusion, the value of $\\dfrac{dy}{dx}$ at $x=3$ is $-\\dfrac{4}{145}$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"$y=\\arctan\\left(-4x\\right)$\n\n**Evaluate $\\dfrac{dy}{dx}$ at $x=3$.**\n\n[[☃ expression 1]]\n\n*Use an exact expression.*","images":{},"widgets":{"expression 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"answerForms":[{"considered":"correct","form":false,"key":0,"simplify":false,"value":"-\\frac{4}{145}"}],"buttonSets":["basic","prealgebra"],"functions":["f","g","h"],"times":false},"static":false,"type":"expression","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
